  "summary": "Single-cell and spatial profiling of immune and tissue compartments across infection, skin, vascular, and autoimmune disease; drivers of rise unestablished.",
  "synthesis": "Activity centers on single-cell and spatial transcriptomic profiling of immune and stromal compartments across disease contexts. Items span pediatric malaria monocyte-T cell interactions, cutaneous T cell lymphoma subtypes from 244 scRNA-seq samples, and a neutrophil atlas integrating 1 million transcriptomes from 781 samples across 43 datasets. Tissue-level studies include carotid atherosclerosis profiled with CosMx spatial transcriptomics, hidradenitis suppurativa keratinocyte states, COPD immune-fibrotic signaling across 101,009 cells, and preeclampsia FOLR2+ macrophages. Several items are reviews, including long-lived plasma cells and PD-1 signaling in autoimmunity. The signal rose 3.3-fold, with 14 published and 2 preprint items. The items do not establish drivers of this increase, and no code or industry signals are present.",
